# Release battery evidence repair

Issue: [91](https://github.com/KatsuJinCode/decko-ts/issues/91).
Status: implementation and local regression checks saved; independent
adversarial review and full release battery remain pending.

## Reproduced failure

The former caller reduced process termination to whether a runner started.
Its classifier consequently returned `PASS` for a process with exit 1 and
passing counters, and for one passing assertion plus three skipped assertions.
The aggregate also accepted `BASELINE` failures as a clean release check.
The old stages omitted numerous Node suites and the actor-capture preflight.

The actual old classifier/caller-expression results, using synthetic inputs
without starting its expensive stages, are retained in
[before.json](release-battery-evidence-2026-10-30.before.json). The old source
SHA-256 is `ca98301d98fe7cf6763a3909d656ecdca2952bc25663760a1aaa67f83cd5ca65`.

## Changed behavior

The replacement retains exit, signal and spawn-error facts; machine reports,
raw process output and selected source hashes remain separate evidence.
Missing reports do not fall back to console text. Files and assertion counts
must reconcile with the selected inventory. Failed, skipped, pending,
interrupted or incomplete required evidence cannot pass. Historical failure
attribution is retained, while any baseline failure prevents a passing battery.

The plan comes from tracked and unignored checkout files and the existing
import classifier. Node and Vitest each execute their selected file inventory
once, with explicitly listed benchmark investigations excluded from this local
battery. The actual CLI admission inventory is retained in
[admission.json](release-battery-evidence-2026-10-30.admission.json); discovery
does not mean those tests ran. An unsuccessful stage does not omit a later
stage. Source bytes and capture inputs are checked for changes during a run.

The actor-bound capture validator and independently supplied expectation file
are required before the full battery starts. No such fresh qualified capture
was supplied in this repair. The actual default CLI therefore returned exit 3,
reported capture evidence `INCOMPLETE`, started neither framework stage and
reported `batteryPassed: false`. Scoped preflight modes explicitly state that
no test-battery verdict was produced.

Standalone child launches remove the inherited `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` field.
An actual nested-runner fixture exposed a recursion warning and zero executed
tests before this boundary correction. Another fixture exposed Windows
file-URL loading through a CommonJS configuration lookup; the generated Vitest
configuration now resolves its ESM entry. Both corrected paths were exercised
by real local child processes, without browser windows or external requests.

## Verification and limits

The final focused Node invocation passed 56 assertions, failed 0, cancelled 0,
skipped 0 and left 0 todo. These are checker regression assertions, not a port
completion score. The raw TAP is retained in
[node-tests.tap](release-battery-evidence-2026-10-30.node-tests.tap).
It includes actual failing/spawn-error children, byte-preserving output,
actual Node pass/partial-skip reports, an actual Vitest pass report, missing
machine reports, later-stage execution, inventory discovery and refusal to
start a full battery without capture admission.

TypeScript checking exited 0. The scoped platform-command scanner inspected
the four changed runner/test modules and found zero platform-specific command
hits. Exact source hashes, tool versions, raw platform output, CLI output and
the cache/retry/model boundary are retained in
[checks.json](release-battery-evidence-2026-10-30.checks.json).
Temporary test fixtures were removed after their child processes exited and
each fixture's absence was asserted. Registered `.runtime` diagnostics remain
available; no native database, reference host or deployment was changed.

This package does not validate the full Node/Vitest inventory, qualify a Ruby
reference capture, establish runtime/backend parity, or prove migration,
privacy, recovery or optimization. Independent review must challenge the
frozen checker and its dependencies before any release verdict is quoted.
Issue 91 remains open until that review and the applicable full run are
recorded. The wider acceptance requirements in decision 0013 remain open.

## Independent review qualification

MiniMax Code reviewer1212 independently confirmed the original false passes
are corrected using the real installed Vitest and Node runners. Its six
remaining findings are tracked on issue91. The retained admission artifact
above was generated before the correction commit on a dirty tree: its
`sourceCommit` identifies the parent, while `sourceStatus` and checker hashes
identify the changed bytes. It is a local diagnostic refusal, not evidence that
the parent commit passed a release battery. The saved hashes were subsequently
verified against the correction commit; that does not retroactively make the
earlier execution a clean-commit run.

The first report's interruption wording also needs this qualification: the
installed Vitest 5.0.1 JSON reporter does not emit `wasInterrupted`,
`numRuntimeErrorTestSuites` or `openHandles`. Optional guards do not measure
those facts in its native reports. Nonzero exit, signal, spawn failure and
missing/incomplete reports independently prevent passing in the exercised
cases. A follow-up source-pinned package addresses the remaining review
findings; this historical raw evidence is preserved unchanged.
